# Super-Linter config for the PUSH and RELEASE workflows: development-push,
# main-push and main-release. The PR workflows use .github/super-linter.env
# instead. Two files exist for one reason only: rw-super-linter.yaml set
#
#   VALIDATE_ALL_CODEBASE: ${{ !contains(github.event_name, 'pull_request') }}
#
# so pushes linted the WHOLE codebase while PRs linted only changed files.
# .github/super-linter.env hardcodes false, which is correct for a PR and wrong
# for a push, hence VALIDATE_ALL_CODEBASE=true below. Everything else is a copy
# of that file.
#
# FILTER_REGEX_EXCLUDE is a REGEX, not a glob. The three workflows above used to
# pass filter-regex-exclude: "[src|.github]/**", which is an INVALID regex --
# `/**` is a repetition operator with no operand, so bash `[[ =~ ]]` and grep -E
# both exit 2 ("repetition-operator operand invalid") and the test silently
# counts as "no match". Nothing was ever excluded. Even if it had compiled,
# `[src|.github]` is a character CLASS matching ONE character from that set, not
# the two directory names. The alternation below is the intended meaning; note
# that it EXCLUDES MORE than the old value did, because the old value excluded
# nothing at all. `src/` does not currently exist in this repo, so in practice
# this excludes `.github/`.
#
# Because the old regex was invalid, Super-Linter's file list came out EMPTY and
# the only linters that ever ran on a push were the repo-wide ones (JSCPD,
# PRE_COMMIT). Lint has effectively been a no-op that always passed. Repairing
# the regex therefore does not shrink lint scope, it turns lint ON for the first
# time, which surfaces pre-existing findings.
#
# VALIDATE_JAVASCRIPT_ES=false is one such case. All 11 .js files in this repo
# are upstream nginx njs code (common/etc/nginx/include/*.js and their
# test/unit/*_test.js). They reference the `ngx` njs runtime global, and the repo
# ships no eslint config, so Super-Linter's default config reports 14 `ngx is not
# defined` / unused-var errors in code we did not write. This repo is a fork of
# nginx/nginx-s3-gateway, which is precisely the case the old
# forkedRepoLIntRestriction input existed to handle: do not fail on third-party
# lint errors. It sits beside the JAVASCRIPT_PRETTIER/STANDARD entries already
# disabled for the same reason.
#
# Keys are alphabetically ordered: Super-Linter runs dotenv-linter over this
# file and UnorderedKey is an error. Do NOT add USE_FIND_ALGORITHM -- it is
# rejected alongside VALIDATE_ALL_CODEBASE=false and has burned time before.
FILTER_REGEX_EXCLUDE=(src/.*|\.github/.*)
IGNORE_GITIGNORED_FILES=true
LOG_LEVEL=WARN
VALIDATE_ALL_CODEBASE=true
VALIDATE_BASH=false
VALIDATE_BASH_EXEC=false
VALIDATE_BIOME_FORMAT=false
VALIDATE_BIOME_LINT=false
VALIDATE_CHECKOV=false
VALIDATE_CLOUDFORMATION=false
VALIDATE_EDITORCONFIG=false
VALIDATE_GITLEAKS=false
VALIDATE_JAVASCRIPT_ES=false
VALIDATE_JAVASCRIPT_PRETTIER=false
VALIDATE_JAVASCRIPT_STANDARD=false
VALIDATE_JSON_PRETTIER=false
VALIDATE_MARKDOWN=false
VALIDATE_MARKDOWN_PRETTIER=false
VALIDATE_NATURAL_LANGUAGE=false
VALIDATE_SHELL_SHFMT=false
VALIDATE_SPELL_CODESPELL=false
VALIDATE_TERRAFORM_TFLINT=false
VALIDATE_TRIVY=false
VALIDATE_TYPESCRIPT_PRETTIER=false
VALIDATE_TYPESCRIPT_STANDARD=false
VALIDATE_YAML_PRETTIER=false
